Ran read.table on the raw table to see what was going in:

  > read.table("inputs/data/cases-v0.tsv", header = TRUE, sep = "\t")
  Error in read.table("inputs/data/cases-v0.tsv") :
    line 4 did not have 10 elements

At that point I opened cases-v0.tsv in an editor. The header line reads

  case_id  family  params    lower  upper  n  seed  mean_tol  sd_tol

but there is a stray TAB between "params" and "lower" — the parser reads
10 columns from the header and 9 from every data row, and blows up at
the first data row (line 4 after the two comment lines).

Root cause: header typo in cases-v0.tsv adds a phantom 10th column, and
everything downstream cascades from that. Everything else in the
traceback is a symptom of the parser giving read_cases a malformed
frame, which the sampler then tried to sample from.

Note: the newer cases.tsv shipped with the current tree does NOT have
this bug. cases-v0.tsv is deprecated and should probably be deleted;
it's only kept in inputs/notes/ because I hadn't decided yet whether to
archive it. Do not source ars.R against cases-v0.tsv.
